# Per-repo divergence from the shared build, included last by the distributed
# Makefile. The shared file is distribute-owned and reset on every push, so
# anything repo-specific belongs here.

# build-all builds only the host target in the gate.
#
# harrow links PostgreSQL's parser through pg_query_go, which is cgo, so
# CGO_ENABLED stays 1 (see .goreleaser.yml). The shared build-all then runs
# goreleaser across the whole matrix, and that matrix includes darwin — which
# needs a darwin C toolchain. The gate image ships gcc and no osxcross, so the
# darwin leg fails with `C compiler "clang" not found` every single run. It is
# not a defect in this repo's code and no change here can make a linux container
# produce a cgo darwin binary.
#
# So the gate builds what it can honestly build. This is a REAL reduction in
# coverage of the build matrix and is recorded as such: nothing verifies that
# harrow still compiles for darwin. Restoring it needs a macOS runner in the
# release workflow, or osxcross in the gate image — until one of those exists,
# a darwin break in a cgo call site would be caught at release time, not here.
#
# The release configuration is untouched: .goreleaser.yml still declares the
# full matrix for a runner that can satisfy it.
.PHONY: build-all
build-all: pre-build
	$(GORELEASER) build --single-target --snapshot --clean
